    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374-a1">

                <pb facs="0669" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg569"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Salisbury to Mr. Hoppin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 2,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 27th ultimo, informing me that you had on the
                    evening of the preceding day received a further telegram from Mr. Evarts in
                    relation to the delay of Her Majesty’s Government in replying to the claim put
                    forward by the United States Government in connection with the occurrences at
                    Fortune Bay in January, 1878, and I have to state to you with reference thereto
                    that the report of the law officers of the Crown upon the case has now been
                    received, and that therefore the reply of Her Majesty’s Government will be sent
                    with the least possible delay, having regard to the question under
                    consideration.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>SALISBURY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
